Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:28:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: Don't free a job's command twice when its
 stream is rejected

After a rejected command stream on the iPad 5, the next exec in another
process oopses in free_bprm with a bad rss-counter. slub_debug reports
"Object already free" on kmalloc-512: the object was allocated and freed
in pvr_fw_cmd_init(), then freed again from pvr_job_put().

When stream parsing fails, pvr_job_process_stream() frees the command.
The caller then releases the job, whose release path frees it again.
Clear the command pointer and length after freeing the rejected command.

Upstream has the same code. Affects every PowerVR device.

Fixes: eaf01ee5ba28 ("drm/imagination: Implement job submission and scheduling")

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_job.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_job.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_job.c
index 95c5d2e..48a1cbc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_job.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_job.c
@@ -79,8 +79,11 @@ pvr_job_process_stream(struct pvr_device *pvr_dev, const struct pvr_stream_cmd_d
 	job->cmd_len = cmd_defs->dest_size;
 
 	err = pvr_stream_process(pvr_dev, cmd_defs, stream, stream_size, job->cmd);
-	if (err)
+	if (err) {
 		kfree(job->cmd);
+		job->cmd = NULL;
+		job->cmd_len = 0;
+	}
 
 	return err;
 }

